<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Agder</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom on Norway's southern tip whose king, according to the sagas, fought Harald Fairhair at Hafrsfjord.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Agder, the southernmost coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, was a small kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>. The sagas link it with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vestfold">Vestfold</a> dynasty through Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asa-haraldsdottir">Åsa</a>, daughter of a king of Agder and mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halfdan-the-black">Halfdan the Black</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Agder faced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skagerrak">Skagerrak</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and lived by farming, fishing and sea trade. Its rulers are known only from late saga tradition, and the boundaries of the kingdom are uncertain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heimskringla">Heimskringla</a> says that Kjotve the Rich, king of Agder, joined the western coalition defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hafrsfjord">Hafrsfjord</a>, traditionally around 872. Agder then passed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/agder.jpg" alt="Agder" width="320" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Odd Jarle Jørgensen · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steaming_away_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Agder</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=agder" aria-label="Agder on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4850 214 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Agder lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5170 470L5225 425"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5170 470h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5170 470h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=agder">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
